[2026-05-10T14:14:32.677Z] [INFO] 2026-05-10T14:14:32.676277Z DEBUG session_loop{thread_id=019e122f-ee66-7f30-b159-6f1cfd807d4a}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input_with_turn_context" submission.id="019e122f-eee6-7e63-be1c-68a309e886fc" codex.op="user_input_with_turn_context"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019e122f-ee66-7f30-b159-6f1cfd807d4a turn.id=019e122f-eee6-7e63-be1c-68a309e886fc model=gpt-5.5 codex.turn.reasoning_effort=xhigh}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: Output item item=Reasoning { id: "rs_07288006065bfb7f016a0092b889c88191ba4c2f993dc511a0", summary: [SummaryText { text: "**Addressing PR updates**\n\nI need to figure out that PR #58 is an active follow-up since PR #50 has been merged and can't receive more commits. It’s crucial to mention the exact URLs. I have concerns about whether we updated the body of PR 50 after merging to reflect test results that didn't apply to the commit. We created the body for PR 58, but should we revert or adjust PR 50's body to avoid misleading claims? Accuracy is really important here!" }, SummaryText { text: "**Updating PR details**\n\nI need to update the body of PR 50. I’m considering whether we should edit the merged PR body to remove the dictionary fix, but maybe it’s better to maintain its integrity. Instead, I'll change PR 50's body to its earlier version and include a note like \"Post-merge follow-up: #58.\" Since it’s merged, the body should accurately reflect the state of that merge, especially since it currently includes updates not in PR 50. Getting this right is important!" }, SummaryText { text: "**Considering PR edits**\n\nI’m thinking about whether I should edit the PR50 body or at least add a comment. I could use the command to edit it with the original content, excluding merge and fix lines from earlier. After merging, though, it seems some tests might have failed, and the info from #51 is now included, which complicates things. I can update the body to reflect the current state but note that it's not critical. Keeping it clean is good!" }, SummaryText { text: "**Adjusting PR body**\n\nI’m planning to use the command to edit the PR50 body with the original content and a note. I don't want to overdo it, so I could simply add a \"Post-merge note\" section. My idea for the body is to include fixes related to #23, the original changes in bullet points, and checks from the implementation. Plus, I want to mention that PR58 resolves the conflicts and compatibility issues after merging PR50, and a screenshot will be included too." }], content: None, encrypted_content: Some("gAAAAABqAJLIidG_N1Gg4v1EKSttVSjRv1FoRJqhV3_n7tv7FfVSio4sFAl0xb_7A2JNPB2DrB1Fu4ZZ6HirSL3JjNPj3COhIuv_Aj5Qj91sW9YA4rZGm836hRtZMOF5kgPKZz8hGD6sDKVlbPx3i0ssl1dWhQPWzWoAy--iWx1_llzlsCwRNMeTpH-18CCSnBvoq5pHneez75FexqXqpf97OW956btBiyNgyNQ3AA34Yc5i8bGRGxEFA7E97NKbuzRMtGiunjJ1TED7bxUQjTLc8pdbVzL6s1-QoTqhp8Wo09yS7YSqES1AD25VaYdWjFwBTc1eJvBNvUsfj7RrjTznVjrOXKLluM8TBNBbgFw162gCPMVQNLL87TnGsATOV-lyKRAhIPaWGyQ2ha5l-8cMUqIpqp-x_Zi4QSaK0CiXnONE2qGSh8aZTzekLlWqR5FVTi4cF8Ga6qBatj2l-vWpdFe_vNsy0xiRbn4YJv6ZENjxcJ6aVLH5BuUFaKsILChi8zACT-Q2bEPOWmBnIF64G47vcTtvdEpLyKzvMzRIxkRCyL09Lvg-1hTgOeTOja4oSf5DHFMxzTqKVO4rXN-2phLLiR4tA7afhM1-YHCop3_JJqA3ApAc69KlN3PN5SYjzvcRdR6Q7xBTXXBivVPyO_k6d4xSYpJgz5TksSH9zlqfs2VbhwQkDfBWJ-FSIQz-v8Wp7WpljGg4QpF5gYzx19XZLOjHEQqELDEFxK17aeSGh_4MPK_vSDTMryZfj4uNUVgukuiGfv0jiq_bEtBi_9u-YplOX84gY2bDQWnpfJH7KMxTHLfIYazlk-mz8YL_TAaE3oRjtLR7WF2OvoNITjbsWebikcdiEVyxrPzxNAI28B9Cr-7ipMujKpwyCXDfA1jDOp2ErsAKFVvdytT0eh8BfA3aEVdl2iK3r0Wi4_mWVIyWG8uh-moqbUBKbMo2LcuouwlDSty4Zh8B2T9wdTA-xblNiVVIr8PJDiznoa9ydyC9yibms6g758ne5JnHLQ9RpiVNNIvNkILyDX-sseCzUxBZOvF7g4yV-otl-yu-VTXzMiF_ZvD2NohR4U7BOPBwn8HsvcgMXs--l4UXrn-89_r1N-Gw6AZjF3u6XmywxivfJlQxQCn7D5xVj-XlY4YCLCoG8lqXIaYlj_GhP0y6zraXIhSy4AJ3v4BVEyLRtcEVnhqWncgvN9KD9DQ9bQ5ZnQjCjvfQvaUtQNg39ngda7xgVoehbW3pCSnxv4zXdF2oFXJIBHcIy2_BqUHokJmIVDa6l6LOign6ZjSIyIWkw_rBe7t4qXMUVwelYFEBAAvq4aDW_pkVuD3MsMff8-KDireXxG8ZCp_T7zm76QzwRR-n0tYN0m_PsvvJxPK